ler CPA | Co-CEO, Co-President & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 25 people. Revenue per employee of $10.5M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $5.1M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $373K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["LTC Properties, Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $2.4B market cap on $263M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $129M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 49 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.15\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 6.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.3%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.0% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 3.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 38% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.376090239467439},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants moni